WEBVTT

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:02.176
It's had tacks in it, and splinters,

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:03.496
and boards torn up,

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:06.120
and places with no carpet on the floor."

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:09.816
Langston Hughes is making
a metaphor that compares

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:13.456
a hard life to a wrecked house
you still have to live in.

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:16.176
Those splinters and tacks feel real,

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:18.976
they hurt your own feet
and your own heart,

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:21.576
but the mother
is describing her life here,

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:23.296
not her actual house.

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:27.056
And hunger, and cold,
exhausting work and poverty

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:29.566
are what's also inside those splinters.